Local/parameter base names derive from the type name via an acronym-aware
lowercaser: an all-caps name lowercases whole. A trailing digit must not split
the acronym, so DB2 lowercases to db2 (like DB → db), not dB2. This pins that
behavior for a capital+digit type name.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
output: plumb_gen.go
-- example.com/app/a.go --
package app

type DB2 struct{}

//plumb:build
func NewDB2() *DB2 { return &DB2{} }

//plumb:build
func Use(db *DB2) int { return 0 }
